Identify is easily hands-down the most useful spell
in the game, so useful that it would be worth casting
a useless level-1 spell in order to exercise the skill
and so gain the ability to cast identify -- if the level-1
spells in that school were useless, that is, but in
fact the light spell (in its own right more useful than
75% of the other spells in the game) is in that
same school, so you can practice by casting that.

> > Is magic missile significantly better as a spell
> > than the wand (other than not having to count
> > charges)?
>
> It's a huge difference. The wand is crap, in my book.

The wand of magic missile can be real boon in
Sokoban, since it can shoot past boulders.
(Certain monsters, if they happen to get
generated behind a boulder you're pushing,
in a narrow space, will never move on their
own, as near as I can tell, or at least you can't
count on it.)  I assume the spell can do the same
thing, but for this purpose the wand is adequate.

